{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AtC7YPG5NoehpY5u7jKhJq","type":"tool_result","content":".:\n.\n..\n.ard\n.ard-input\n.dockerignore\n.git\n.github\n.gitignore\n.goreleaser.yaml\nCLAUDE.md\nDockerfile\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\ncmd\ndeploy\ndocs\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nmkdocs.yml\n\n.github/workflows:\n.\n..\nbot-commits.yml\nci.yml\nversion.yml\n\ndocs:\n.\n..\nTODO.md\nlayout.md\nproposal.md\nrunbooks\nsite\n\ndocs/runbooks:\n.\n..\nonboard-repo.md\npages-setup.md\nrelease.md\n# GoReleaser v2 config for ard. Releases run from the release workflow on the\n# v* tags version.yml pushes; `make release-check` runs it locally as a snapshot.\nversion: 2\nproject_name: ard\n\nbuilds:\n  - id: ard\n    main: ./cmd/ard\n    binary: ard\n    env:\n      - CGO_ENABLED=0\n    goos: [darwin, linux]\n    goarch: [arm64, amd64]\n    flags:\n      - -trimpath\n    ldflags:\n      - -s -w -X main.version={{.Tag}}\n    mod_timestamp: \"{{ .CommitTimestamp }}\"\n\narchives:\n  - id: ard\n    formats: [tar.gz]\n    name_template: \"ard_{{ .Version }}_{{ .Os }}_{{ .Arch }}\"\n\nchecksum:\n  name_template: checksums.txt\n\n# version.yml already created the (notes-only) release; add files to it.\nrelease:\n  mode: keep-existing\n  github:\n    owner: albertcbrown\n    name: ard\n\nhomebrew_casks:\n  - name: ard\n    directory: Casks\n    homepage: https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n    description: Autonomous repository development agents driven by GitHub issues\n    # The token comes from the environment of the release workflow.\n    repository:\n      owner: albertcbrown\n      name: homebrew-tap\n      token: \"{{ .Env.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN }}\"\n    url:\n      template: \"https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/releases/download/{{ .Tag }}/{{ .ArtifactName }}\"\n    dependencies:\n      - formula: git\n    caveats: |\n      ard runs agents that need the claude CLI and either CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n      or an API key in the environment.\n    # Accepted risk (see docs/proposal.md): the binary is not signed or notarized\n    # yet, so Gatekeeper's quarantine flag is cleared after install.\n    hooks:\n      post:\n        install: |\n          system_command \"/usr/bin/xattr\",\n                         args: [\"-dr\", \"com.apple.quarantine\", \"#{staged_path}/ard\"]\n(eval):1: no matches found: .github/workflows/release*\n# Release runbook\n\n`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## Seed tag\n\nAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\ngit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n```\n\nUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n\n## Settings checklist\n\n- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n\n## Dry run to live\n\nEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n\n## Bumps and the module path\n\nLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n\n## Recovery\n\n- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\nREADME.md:1:# ard — automated repository development\nREADME.md:9:## How it works\nREADME.md:26:## Configuration by convention\nREADME.md:42:## Development\nREADME.md:54:## License\ndocs/proposal.md:1:# ard: Automated Repository Development\ndocs/proposal.md:5:## Summary\ndocs/proposal.md:22:## Architecture\ndocs/proposal.md:44:## Stack\ndocs/proposal.md:48:## Label state machine\ndocs/proposal.md:95:## The .ard/ contract\ndocs/proposal.md:157:## Open issues\ndocs/proposal.md:171:## Scanners\ndocs/proposal.md:245:## Triage loop\ndocs/proposal.md:286:## Executors and the Reaper\ndocs/proposal.md:332:## Worker loop\ndocs/proposal.md:352:## Reviewer loop\ndocs/proposal.md:385:## Merger loop\ndocs/proposal.md:410:## PR watch loop\ndocs/proposal.md:424:## Configuration\ndocs/proposal.md:495:## Guardrails\ndocs/proposal.md:522:## Gaps in the original sketch\ndocs/proposal.md:542:## Delivery\ndocs/proposal.md:554:## Rollout\ndocs/proposal.md:583:## Open questions\n14:  protected_paths:\n15-    - .github/\n16-    - .ard/config.yaml\n17-    - .ard/scanners/\n18-    - .ard/triage/\n19-    - .ard/workers/\n20-    - .ard/reviewers/\n21-    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n22-    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n3632770 Kubernetes executor, part 1: decision record and proposal update… (#353)\na78e7e0 ard(triage:engineer): #293 Adds a repo-context section to each of the 11 embedded starter prompts… [skip ci]\nea9db63 ard(triage:engineer): #302 Plans a startup GitHub connectivity check, live-run support for a perso… [skip ci]\n0eaa949 ard(triage:lead): #307 This is a docs-only change. It adds a Homebrew install section to the R… [skip ci]\n5b7d0ba ard(triage:lead): #293 This change edits the starter role prompts embedded in internal/roles s… [skip ci]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cad2783-7f2e-46e4-98f8-bdceb598cb1e","uuid":"9a4e29fa-2a61-43b5-91e1-94dbefd1597e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:02:48.815Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".:\n.\n..\n.ard\n.ard-input\n.dockerignore\n.git\n.github\n.gitignore\n.goreleaser.yaml\nCLAUDE.md\nDockerfile\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\ncmd\ndeploy\ndocs\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nmkdocs.yml\n\n.github/workflows:\n.\n..\nbot-commits.yml\nci.yml\nversion.yml\n\ndocs:\n.\n..\nTODO.md\nlayout.md\nproposal.md\nrunbooks\nsite\n\ndocs/runbooks:\n.\n..\nonboard-repo.md\npages-setup.md\nrelease.md\n# GoReleaser v2 config for ard. Releases run from the release workflow on the\n# v* tags version.yml pushes; `make release-check` runs it locally as a snapshot.\nversion: 2\nproject_name: ard\n\nbuilds:\n  - id: ard\n    main: ./cmd/ard\n    binary: ard\n    env:\n      - CGO_ENABLED=0\n    goos: [darwin, linux]\n    goarch: [arm64, amd64]\n    flags:\n      - -trimpath\n    ldflags:\n      - -s -w -X main.version={{.Tag}}\n    mod_timestamp: \"{{ .CommitTimestamp }}\"\n\narchives:\n  - id: ard\n    formats: [tar.gz]\n    name_template: \"ard_{{ .Version }}_{{ .Os }}_{{ .Arch }}\"\n\nchecksum:\n  name_template: checksums.txt\n\n# version.yml already created the (notes-only) release; add files to it.\nrelease:\n  mode: keep-existing\n  github:\n    owner: albertcbrown\n    name: ard\n\nhomebrew_casks:\n  - name: ard\n    directory: Casks\n    homepage: https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n    description: Autonomous repository development agents driven by GitHub issues\n    # The token comes from the environment of the release workflow.\n    repository:\n      owner: albertcbrown\n      name: homebrew-tap\n      token: \"{{ .Env.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN }}\"\n    url:\n      template: \"https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/releases/download/{{ .Tag }}/{{ .ArtifactName }}\"\n    dependencies:\n      - formula: git\n    caveats: |\n      ard runs agents that need the claude CLI and either CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n      or an API key in the environment.\n    # Accepted risk (see docs/proposal.md): the binary is not signed or notarized\n    # yet, so Gatekeeper's quarantine flag is cleared after install.\n    hooks:\n      post:\n        install: |\n          system_command \"/usr/bin/xattr\",\n                         args: [\"-dr\", \"com.apple.quarantine\", \"#{staged_path}/ard\"]\n(eval):1: no matches found: .github/workflows/release*\n# Release runbook\n\n`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## Seed tag\n\nAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\ngit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n```\n\nUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n\n## Settings checklist\n\n- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n\n## Dry run to live\n\nEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n\n## Bumps and the module path\n\nLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n\n## Recovery\n\n- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\nREADME.md:1:# ard — automated repository development\nREADME.md:9:## How it works\nREADME.md:26:## Configuration by convention\nREADME.md:42:## Development\nREADME.md:54:## License\ndocs/proposal.md:1:# ard: Automated Repository Development\ndocs/proposal.md:5:## Summary\ndocs/proposal.md:22:## Architecture\ndocs/proposal.md:44:## Stack\ndocs/proposal.md:48:## Label state machine\ndocs/proposal.md:95:## The .ard/ contract\ndocs/proposal.md:157:## Open issues\ndocs/proposal.md:171:## Scanners\ndocs/proposal.md:245:## Triage loop\ndocs/proposal.md:286:## Executors and the Reaper\ndocs/proposal.md:332:## Worker loop\ndocs/proposal.md:352:## Reviewer loop\ndocs/proposal.md:385:## Merger loop\ndocs/proposal.md:410:## PR watch loop\ndocs/proposal.md:424:## Configuration\ndocs/proposal.md:495:## Guardrails\ndocs/proposal.md:522:## Gaps in the original sketch\ndocs/proposal.md:542:## Delivery\ndocs/proposal.md:554:## Rollout\ndocs/proposal.md:583:## Open questions\n14:  protected_paths:\n15-    - .github/\n16-    - .ard/config.yaml\n17-    - .ard/scanners/\n18-    - .ard/triage/\n19-    - .ard/workers/\n20-    - .ard/reviewers/\n21-    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n22-    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n3632770 Kubernetes executor, part 1: decision record and proposal update… (#353)\na78e7e0 ard(triage:engineer): #293 Adds a repo-context section to each of the 11 embedded starter prompts… [skip ci]\nea9db63 ard(triage:engineer): #302 Plans a startup GitHub connectivity check, live-run support for a perso… [skip ci]\n0eaa949 ard(triage:lead): #307 This is a docs-only change. It adds a Homebrew install section to the R… [skip ci]\n5b7d0ba ard(triage:lead): 