{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013jjwpoSZzoWDVmcDeZA1if","type":"tool_result","content":"./.goreleaser.yaml\n./Makefile\n./deploy/test-release.sh\n./docs/layout.md\n4:.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lts-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test agent-image agent-image-test docs-check release-check\n66:# Validates .goreleaser.yaml and builds a snapshot release of all four targets\n67:# (needs goreleaser v2 and python3; not part of `make test`).\n68:release-check:\n69:\tdeploy/test-release.sh\n0eaa949 ard(triage:lead): #307 This is a docs-only change. It adds a Homebrew install section to the R… [skip ci]\n626b2bf feat: Install ard with Homebrew, part A: GoReleaser config and r… (#306) (#341)\n99a0698 Merge branch 'main' into worker/engineer-306-install-ard-with-homebrew-part-a-gorelea\n096d2db Merge branch 'main' into worker/engineer-306-install-ard-with-homebrew-part-a-gorelea\n84287d5 ard(review:eng-review): #306 The change matches the issue: the GoReleaser v2 config has four targets…\n246ba4d ard(worker:engineer): #306 Adds a GoReleaser v2 config with a Homebrew cask and a `make release-ch…\n2a8379a feat: Install ard with Homebrew, part A: GoReleaser config and r… (#306)\nd98b026 ard(triage:engineer): #306 Adds a GoReleaser v2 config with the Homebrew cask, a `deploy/test-rele… [skip ci]\n8bf8bb3 ard(triage:lead): #306 Adds a GoReleaser configuration with a Homebrew cask definition and a l… [skip ci]\n## Guardrails\n\nAgents with push access read text that strangers can write, so the controls sit in code and permissions, not in prompts.\n\n- **Identity: a GitHub App, not a PAT.** Installation tokens expire hourly and are scoped to contents, issues and pull requests (read and write), plus checks (r\n- **The GitHub client never follows redirects.** A redirect can turn a write into a silent GET, replay it into another repository, or carry the token to another\n- **Agents hold no GitHub token.** The executor does. The agent's environment has only its model credential: an API key or a subscription OAuth token; in Kubern\n- **Isolated agent pod.** The agent container holds only its model credential. `pre` and `post` run as a different UID. A ValidatingAdmissionPolicy enforces `sh\n- **Result key and listener.** `post` serves one route, guarded by a per-pod 32-byte key mounted only in `post` and kept in memory by the controller, over plain\n- **Result untar is the boundary.** The controller treats the pulled tar as hostile: `os.Root`; no hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplica\n- **Cluster.** The jobs namespace has Pod Security `restricted`; the job SA has no roles and no token; `enableServiceLinks: false`, non-root, drop ALL, RuntimeD\n- **Residual risks (Kubernetes).** The model credential sits in a per-job Secret in etcd, so etcd encryption at rest is required. The tee'd stdout is agent-writ\n- **Intake is configurable (decided, #2).** `intake` is either `all` (every human-filed issue enters, no label) or `label` (only issues with the configured labe\n- **Untrusted text is passed as data.** Issue bodies, comments and PR text go to the agent as files the prompt labels as untrusted input, never spliced into the\n- **Planted repo config does not steer agents.** A branch can carry CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, `.claude/` settings, hooks, skills, agents or a `.mcp.json`. The Claud\n- **Agents write only their own files.** Close-out lets a job change under `.ard/<issue#>/` only its own role file and what its role owns (a `plan.md` section, \n- **Role files are human-owned.** The diff guard and the committer's code lane reject any worker change under `.ard/` or `.github/` (so `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ar\n- **The tag-writing credential is separate.** Only the `tag` job of `version.yml`, in the `release` environment, holds a token that can push tags, from a releas\n- **Merges are gated.** The merger lands a PR only when every review passed and required checks (read from the branch rules API) are green on an up-to-date bran\n- **Agent text cannot close issues.** Agent text in a commit message, PR title or PR body has closing references neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`: \"Fixes\n- **Worker diffs are scanned.** The worker's diff is checked for known credential values and for secret patterns on the lines the job added. A hit holds the cha\n- **Committed output is redacted.** Close-out strips known secret values, and replaces the controller host's paths (see \"All agent output is committed too\") wit\n- **Budgets.** Every job has a dollar cap (`max_budget_usd`) and a hard timeout; every role and the whole repo have a daily dollar cap. The caps are enforced at\n- **Concurrency.** `max_pods` (default 3) caps every job together, and at most one triage job runs per issue at a time, because triage roles share `plan.md`; no\n- **Kill switch.** Four sources stop new claims, scanner runs (filing and autoclose), stale closes and merges: a local pause file `~/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` \n- **Observability.** Every claim, close-out and failure is an event in local state. A daily digest on the pinned status issue shows queue depth by label, jobs r\n\n| Skip a scanner over X open issues | One noisy scanner still floods the queue; no cost ceiling | Per-scanner cap, plus a global cap and a daily spend cap |\n\n## Delivery\n\nHow ard itself is built, published and deployed. Jenkins and Argo CD do the work; the cluster-specific wiring (the Jenkins job definitions and their publishing \n\n- **Checks.** The Jenkins multibranch job `ard-ci` builds every same-repository branch and pull request, `worker/*` branches included, but never forks, with `ma\n- **Publish.** A green `main` build starts `ard-build`, whose Jenkinsfile is not in this repository, so nothing merged here can reach its credentials. It builds\n- **Agent image.** The default `ard-agent` image (`deploy/agent/Dockerfile`: the `claude` CLI pinned to `claude.TestedVersion` with per-architecture checksums, \n- **Deploy.** A deploy job verifies the signature and the revision label, checks the new commit descends from the pinned one, and pins the digest and commit in \n- **Versioning ([#183](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/183)).** `version.yml` gives every first-parent merge to `main` an annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` and \n- **Release.** An annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` (`git tag -a`) builds that commit with `VERSION=vX.Y.Z`, pushes `:vX.Y.Z` and moves `:latest` when it is the highest ve\n- **Kill switch in a cluster.** `kubectl -n <namespace> exec deploy/ard-<instance> -- touch /home/ard/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` pauses `ard serve`; `rm` resume\n\n## Rollout\n\nStart on one repo (albertcbrown/ard itself, dogfooding; decided, #6) with the local executor and a human approval gate; humans merge until Gate 2, then the merg\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    P0[\"Phase 0: Skeleton<br/>controller and config<br/>label bootstrap<br/>committer, local executor<br/>cve and stale scanners<br/>dry-run mode\"] -->|\"Gate 1:\n    P1 -->|\"Gate 2: 10 merged PRs, failures under 10%\"| P2[\"Phase 2: All roles<br/>all triage roles<br/>all four reviewers<br/>review fix rounds<br/>merger loop\n    P2 -->|\"Gate 3: 50% merged with no human code edits\"| P3[\"Phase 3: Scale<br/>k8s executor<br/>second repo<br/>shared roles repo<br/>budgets and digest\"]\n    P3 --> P4[\"Phase 4: Docs and site<br/>user documentation<br/>GitHub Pages site\"]\n    P4 --> P5[\"Phase 5: Distribution<br/>versioned releases<br/>Homebrew cask\"]\n```\n\nPhases 4 and 5 have no gate: Phase 4 ([#178](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/178)) writes the user documentation and publishes it as a GitHub Pages s\n\n**Where it runs (decided, #5; amended for the soak, [#144](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/144)).** `ard serve` runs live on the owner's Mac with the\n\n**One `ard serve` per repository.** To run ard on another repository, start a second `ard serve` for it; limits and credentials belong to each process (see Conf\n\nPhase 0 runs in dry-run: the controller logs every issue, label and commit it would make, and does none of them. Dry-run keeps its own state (`~/.ard/state-dryr\n\n| Metric | Proposed target |\n| --- | --- |\n| Duplicate issues filed | 0 |\n| Executor failure rate | under 10% of jobs |\n| Scanner issues closed by an ard PR with no human code edits | 50% by the end of Phase 2 |\n| Median time from `ard:pending` to a ready PR | under 1 working day |\n| Cost per merged PR | measured in Phase 1 from the Total row of the issue's cost table; daily budget set from it |\n\n```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n\n```bash\nmake build   # builds bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n```\n\nContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n## License\n\n[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cad2783-7f2e-46e4-98f8-bdceb598cb1e","uuid":"fcb83120-d0cf-4bcc-a4e1-b34c0357251a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T20:02:53.983Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"./.goreleaser.yaml\n./Makefile\n./deploy/test-release.sh\n./docs/layout.md\n4:.PHONY: build test lint fmt clean cve-fixtures lts-fixtures lint-scanner-fixtures chart-test image-test agent-image agent-image-test docs-check release-check\n66:# Validates .goreleaser.yaml and builds a snapshot release of all four targets\n67:# (needs goreleaser v2 and python3; not part of `make test`).\n68:release-check:\n69:\tdeploy/test-release.sh\n0eaa949 ard(triage:lead): #307 This is a docs-only change. It adds a Homebrew install section to the R… [skip ci]\n626b2bf feat: Install ard with Homebrew, part A: GoReleaser config and r… (#306) (#341)\n99a0698 Merge branch 'main' into worker/engineer-306-install-ard-with-homebrew-part-a-gorelea\n096d2db Merge branch 'main' into worker/engineer-306-install